    ('b01521d4-d283-46be-8ebc-91eb93147d16', 5, $$She has a new dress.$$),
    ('b01521d4-d283-46be-8ebc-91eb93147d16', 6, $$Why is the old man laughing?$$),
    ('b01521d4-d283-46be-8ebc-91eb93147d16', 7, $$He read a good joke.$$),
    ('b01521d4-d283-46be-8ebc-91eb93147d16', 8, $$Why is the lady smiling?$$),
    ('b01521d4-d283-46be-8ebc-91eb93147d16', 9, $$Her children are reading quietly.$$),
    ('b01521d4-d283-46be-8ebc-91eb93147d16', 10, $$What is this lady feeling? I think she is feeling shy.$$),
    ('b0f2a9ab-2326-4686-aa36-f8d57c859345', 0, $$Wewak Boy$$),
    ('b0f2a9ab-2326-4686-aa36-f8d57c859345', 1, $$My heart is with the place where I was born. I am from Wewak. Where I am from, is part of who I am.$$),
    ('b0f2a9ab-2326-4686-aa36-f8d57c859345', 2, $$I grew up in Wewak. I spent most of my boyhood days in that town.$$),
    ('b0f2a9ab-2326-4686-aa36-f8d57c859345', 3, $$I first went to school in Wewak. These were some of the most enjoyable times in my life.$$),
    ('b0f2a9ab-2326-4686-aa36-f8d57c859345', 4, $$When I was sixteen years old, I was very sick with menangitis. I was in the hospital for ten months.$$),
    ('b0f2a9ab-2326-4686-aa36-f8d57c859345', 5, $$I recovered, but my inner ear became damaged, meaning that I lost my hearing. I became deaf.$$),
    ('b0f2a9ab-2326-4686-aa36-f8d57c859345', 6, $$As a young man with a hearing disability, my greatest interest was playing sports.$$),
    ('b0f2a9ab-2326-4686-aa36-f8d57c859345', 7, $$I love playing soccer and rugby. My deafness does not stop me from playing the sports that I love.$$),
    ('b0f2a9ab-2326-4686-aa36-f8d57c859345', 8, $$I am happy to grow in my skill with sign language. I love to use sign language to communicate. I love the deaf world.$$),
    ('b30b0142-c791-4a52-9a5e-a4d4e4f4bf2a', 0, $$Some people sell things at the market. I sell food at the market.$$),
    ('b30b0142-c791-4a52-9a5e-a4d4e4f4bf2a', 1, $$Some people sell things in a store. I sell things in a sports store.$$),
    ('b30b0142-c791-4a52-9a5e-a4d4e4f4bf2a', 2, $$Some people drive things. I drive a digger.$$),
    ('b30b0142-c791-4a52-9a5e-a4d4e4f4bf2a', 3, $$Some people fly things. I fly this plane.$$),
    ('b30b0142-c791-4a52-9a5e-a4d4e4f4bf2a', 4, $$Some people fix things in a workshop. I fix this car.$$),
    ('b30b0142-c791-4a52-9a5e-a4d4e4f4bf2a', 5, $$Some people fix things in the Aid Post. I fix Peter’s arm.$$),
    ('b30b0142-c791-4a52-9a5e-a4d4e4f4bf2a', 6, $$Some people grow things in a garden. I grow food in my garden.$$),
    ('b30b0142-c791-4a52-9a5e-a4d4e4f4bf2a', 7, $$Some people make things at home. I am making a bilum.$$),
    ('b30b0142-c791-4a52-9a5e-a4d4e4f4bf2a', 8, $$Some people make things in the village. We are making a house.$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 0, $$I live in the mango tree. I eat lots of ripe fruit in summer.$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 1, $$When my babies are in the nest, I have to be on guard.$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 2, $$Come peep into my nest. See the lovely things I have found.$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 3, $$I love to fly up in the sky, like a plane.$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 4, $$I sit on the tree and look around for some tasty bits of food.$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 5, $$I look to my right. I look to my left.$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 6, $$I love fish. When I spot it, I fly down to pick it up.$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 7, $$With my cawing I call my friends to share the feast with me.$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 8, $$Some people shout at me, “Go away, you noisy bird. ”$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 9, $$Mr Fox likes my singing. He told me so himself.$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 10, $$$$),
    ('b3f503ec-5d7f-4362-bac4-bf6673143813', 11, $$A lion roars. A dog barks. Crows make a lot of noise. So when some people talk loudly we say, “As noisy as a crow”.$$),
    ('b700877a-f0e4-483b-8e9a-e1b4cd726022', 0, $$This is Agnes. She is my teacher.$$),
    ('b700877a-f0e4-483b-8e9a-e1b4cd726022', 1, $$Agnes uses crutches to walk.$$),
    ('b700877a-f0e4-483b-8e9a-e1b4cd726022', 2, $$This is Metobo. He is my favourite radio DJ.$$),
    ('b700877a-f0e4-483b-8e9a-e1b4cd726022', 3, $$He has problems with his eyes.$$),
    ('b700877a-f0e4-483b-8e9a-e1b4cd726022', 4, $$My neighbour is Moraa. She is a farmer.$$),
    ('b700877a-f0e4-483b-8e9a-e1b4cd726022', 5, $$Moraa cannot hear. She speaks using Sign language.$$),
    ('b700877a-f0e4-483b-8e9a-e1b4cd726022', 6, $$This is Osero. He is the best football player at my school.$$),
    ('b700877a-f0e4-483b-8e9a-e1b4cd726022', 7, $$Osero has no hands. But he scores many goals for our team!$$),
    ('b72f5939-1786-49f6-ada2-543d51f87099', 0, $$Who will eat these baby fish?$$),
    ('b72f5939-1786-49f6-ada2-543d51f87099', 1, $$A shark will eat these baby fish.$$),
    ('b72f5939-1786-49f6-ada2-543d51f87099', 2, $$Who will eat these mice?$$),
    ('b72f5939-1786-49f6-ada2-543d51f87099', 3, $$A snake will eat these mice.$$),
    ('b72f5939-1786-49f6-ada2-543d51f87099', 4, $$Who will eat these worms?$$),
    ('b72f5939-1786-49f6-ada2-543d51f87099', 5, $$A bird will eat these worms.$$),
    ('b72f5939-1786-49f6-ada2-543d51f87099', 6, $$Who will eat these insects?$$),
    ('b72f5939-1786-49f6-ada2-543d51f87099', 7, $$A frog will eat these insects.$$),
    ('b72f5939-1786-49f6-ada2-543d51f87099', 8, $$Who will eat these bananas?$$),
    ('b72f5939-1786-49f6-ada2-543d51f87099', 9, $$A monkey will eat these bananas.$$),
    ('b8656f29-a042-4bb7-95de-6da542ed7b8d', 0, $$Nanhi picked up her slate and chalk. She wanted to draw a long, l-o-n-g train.$$),
    ('b8656f29-a042-4bb7-95de-6da542ed7b8d', 1, $$Nanhi first drew an engine which gave out a lot of smoke, for the long, long train.$$),
    ('b8656f29-a042-4bb7-95de-6da542ed7b8d', 2, $$“Oh dear! Now where shall I make the coaches? ” Nanhi wondered, for there was no more space on the slate.$$),
    ('b8656f29-a042-4bb7-95de-6da542ed7b8d', 3, $$Nanhi put the slate and chalk down on the floor and thought.$$),
    ('b8656f29-a042-4bb7-95de-6da542ed7b8d', 4, $$She drew a coach on the floor. Then a second coach, then another, and another, and another... Nanhi just kept drawing.$$),
    ('b8656f29-a042-4bb7-95de-6da542ed7b8d', 5, $$She drew until her chalk ran out. Nanhi got up and took a look. Wow! Her train was as long as the verandah!$$),
    ('b8656f29-a042-4bb7-95de-6da542ed7b8d', 6, $$And off went Nanhi’s train – Chhuk-Chhuk-Chhak, from here to there, so very far!$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 0, $$It was a hot summer day in the dry forest.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 1, $$Little Ant had no water for many days.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 2, $$"I need a drop of water, even if it falls from a leaf," cried Little Ant.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 3, $$But even the dew had dried up.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 4, $$"If I do not have water, I will die," cried Little Ant. "I must go to the river I heard about. "$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 5, $$"The river is full and strong. It will sweep you away," warned a wise squirrel.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 6, $$But Little Ant was extremely thirsty. "I will die if I don't drink some water. "$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 7, $$So, he went to look for the river.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 8, $$He walked past tufts of grass and over dry branches.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 9, $$He walked until he heard water splashing. It was the river! He could hear waves.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 10, $$Little Ant took a long sip of cool water.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 11, $$He was so happy he did not see a wave coming.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 12, $$Little Ant tried to grab some grass floating past him. But he was swept away by the water.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 13, $$"Help me someone. Help me please! " he called.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 14, $$"Quick, climb on," said White Dove, holding a branch in her beak.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 15, $$$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 16, $$"I will stay here until I can thank the dove," decided Little Ant. "I will wait until she comes back to drink. "$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 17, $$As he waited, two boys came to the river. They had their slingshots.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 18, $$"There is a big white dove that comes here to drink," said one boy. "We will have it for supper tonight. "$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 19, $$"I cannot let the boys kill White Dove," thought Little Ant. "But I am so tiny, what can I do? "$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 20, $$Just then White Dove flew down from the tree to drink.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 21, $$$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 22, $$Little Ant had an idea.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 23, $$He jumped onto one boy's foot. Little Ant bit that boy as hard as he could.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 24, $$The boy jumped. "Ouch! " he shouted.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 25, $$White Dove was startled and flew away to safety.$$),
    ('b8b72cfb-8922-41c0-a168-a9c6fd299318', 26, $$That was how Little Ant thanked White Dove for saving him.$$),
    ('bc9486ea-c355-4655-8662-a018f5d5a9aa', 0, $$Look at the animals.$$),
    ('bc9486ea-c355-4655-8662-a018f5d5a9aa', 1, $$Moo$$),
    ('bc9486ea-c355-4655-8662-a018f5d5a9aa', 2, $$Meh Meh$$),
    ('bc9486ea-c355-4655-8662-a018f5d5a9aa', 3, $$The horse says, "Neigh. "$$),
    ('bc9486ea-c355-4655-8662-a018f5d5a9aa', 4, $$The pig says, "Oink, oink. "$$),
    ('bc9486ea-c355-4655-8662-a018f5d5a9aa', 5, $$The chicken says, "Cluck, cluck. "$$),
    ('bc9486ea-c355-4655-8662-a018f5d5a9aa', 6, $$Woof$$),
    ('bc9486ea-c355-4655-8662-a018f5d5a9aa', 7, $$And the farmer says, "Shhh! "$$),
    ('bdcff856-7ae6-4191-9b33-7d9a327742bb', 0, $$Latika, Vidvath and Shubhi were very excited to know that they would go to Gudi Gudi on a vacation.$$),
    ('bdcff856-7ae6-4191-9b33-7d9a327742bb', 1, $$Shubhi and Latika had brought some fruits, but feared that the ants will eat them. Vidvath brought his paratha along as well.$$),
    ('bdcff856-7ae6-4191-9b33-7d9a327742bb', 2, $$Everyone happily went to the station along with Mummy and Papa. The porter took the luggage along.$$),
    ('bdcff856-7ae6-4191-9b33-7d9a327742bb', 3, $$Vidvath, Latika and Shubhi sat on their seats. They had the vegetables and fruits as well which they had brought. Everybody had a great lunch.$$),
    ('bdcff856-7ae6-4191-9b33-7d9a327742bb', 4, $$The train was going over the bridge. Vidvath was very happy to see the water below in the river.$$),
    ('bdcff856-7ae6-4191-9b33-7d9a327742bb', 5, $$Once Shubhi, Latika and Vidvath reached the train station, they went further to the mountains in a bus.$$),
    ('bf26d12c-f74e-44b8-8dd4-50bed0d71aa1', 0, $$I have many friends.$$),
    ('bf26d12c-f74e-44b8-8dd4-50bed0d71aa1', 1, $$Some of my friends are older and...$$),
    ('bf26d12c-f74e-44b8-8dd4-50bed0d71aa1', 2, $$Some of them are younger than me.$$),
    ('bf26d12c-f74e-44b8-8dd4-50bed0d71aa1', 3, $$Some of my friends are old.$$),
    ('bf26d12c-f74e-44b8-8dd4-50bed0d71aa1', 4, $$And some of them are tiny!$$),
    ('bf26d12c-f74e-44b8-8dd4-50bed0d71aa1', 5, $$Some of my friends have tails...$$),
    ('bf26d12c-f74e-44b8-8dd4-50bed0d71aa1', 6, $$Some of my friends have no feet.$$),
    ('bf26d12c-f74e-44b8-8dd4-50bed0d71aa1', 7, $$Some of my friends fly. Some of them swim.$$),
    ('bf26d12c-f74e-44b8-8dd4-50bed0d71aa1', 8, $$Oh! Books are my friends too!$$),
    ('bf26d12c-f74e-44b8-8dd4-50bed0d71aa1', 9, $$But who is my best friend? Who? Who? Who?$$),
    ('bf26d12c-f74e-44b8-8dd4-50bed0d71aa1', 10, $$My mother!!!$$),
    ('bf6fe85c-a533-4922-9492-afc63d992ce5', 0, $$I walk.$$),
