    ('c3864205-a58a-425d-9af2-439c0d61e721', 0, $$One Day, Arrogant bird built nest at the tip of a branch.$$),
    ('c3864205-a58a-425d-9af2-439c0d61e721', 1, $$A crow advised, Its danger! Its not wise to build nest at the tip of the branch. But Arrogant bird didn't listen.$$),
    ('c3864205-a58a-425d-9af2-439c0d61e721', 2, $$One day, the wind blew fiercely. The tree began to shake and nest collapsed.$$),
    ('c3864205-a58a-425d-9af2-439c0d61e721', 3, $$Now Arrogant bird learned lesson that "I will obey wise advises from others".$$),
    ('c82262e3-4cc0-4346-8359-5de22b43827f', 0, $$Excited$$),
    ('c82262e3-4cc0-4346-8359-5de22b43827f', 1, $$Sad$$),
    ('c82262e3-4cc0-4346-8359-5de22b43827f', 2, $$Shy$$),
    ('c82262e3-4cc0-4346-8359-5de22b43827f', 3, $$Scared$$),
    ('c82262e3-4cc0-4346-8359-5de22b43827f', 4, $$Happy$$),
    ('c82262e3-4cc0-4346-8359-5de22b43827f', 5, $$Angry$$),
    ('cb34b41b-3c64-401c-8166-76a0127e2911', 0, $$Pinky is a lovely and intelligent girl.$$),
    ('cb34b41b-3c64-401c-8166-76a0127e2911', 1, $$She goes to school daily with her mother.$$),
    ('cb34b41b-3c64-401c-8166-76a0127e2911', 2, $$Her school building is very big.$$),
    ('cb34b41b-3c64-401c-8166-76a0127e2911', 3, $$She is very keen in studies.$$),
    ('cb34b41b-3c64-401c-8166-76a0127e2911', 4, $$She has a lovely pet dog named, Puppy.$$),
    ('cb34b41b-3c64-401c-8166-76a0127e2911', 5, $$She plays with Puppy when she comes back from school.$$),
    ('ce0f2ffb-f514-417a-8b17-4de70ab8d851', 0, $$We like to visit Grandma’s village.$$),
    ('ce0f2ffb-f514-417a-8b17-4de70ab8d851', 1, $$Grandma has a big mango tree in her garden. Many birds come there.$$),
    ('ce0f2ffb-f514-417a-8b17-4de70ab8d851', 2, $$I like to hide in the mango tree. No one can see me here.$$),
    ('ce0f2ffb-f514-417a-8b17-4de70ab8d851', 3, $$Father looks for me near the well. Mother looks for me near the cowshed. But no one can find me.$$),
    ('ce0f2ffb-f514-417a-8b17-4de70ab8d851', 4, $$Oh no! At last Grandma's dog finds me.$$),
    ('ce0f2ffb-f514-417a-8b17-4de70ab8d851', 5, $$Now I have to climb down Grandma gives me a big hug.$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 0, $$One day three little kittens meet a big dog.$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 1, $$The kittens are scared of the dog.$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 2, $$The little kittens run...$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 3, $$...and the dog follows them.$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 4, $$The little kittens run faster and faster!$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 5, $$The little kittens run into a little bird.$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 6, $$But the little kittens keep on running.$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 7, $$The little kittens run into a little boy.$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 8, $$But the little kittens keep on running.$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 9, $$They run towards a long piece of wood.$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 10, $$“Uh oh! We're in trouble now. ” “Help! Help! ” they cry.$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 11, $$The smiling dog runs up to them. “I'm so happy to run with all of you! ” he says.$$),
    ('cf425be1-d87e-45f8-87af-963cad54e218', 12, $$What a surprise! Now, the little kittens have a new friend.$$),
    ('d18c4245-f14b-4b1d-8eb5-267ee33208bd', 0, $$My cat.$$),
    ('d18c4245-f14b-4b1d-8eb5-267ee33208bd', 1, $$This is my cat.$$),
    ('d18c4245-f14b-4b1d-8eb5-267ee33208bd', 2, $$My cat is big.$$),
    ('d18c4245-f14b-4b1d-8eb5-267ee33208bd', 3, $$It is big and fat.$$),
    ('d18c4245-f14b-4b1d-8eb5-267ee33208bd', 4, $$My cat is black and white.$$),
    ('d18c4245-f14b-4b1d-8eb5-267ee33208bd', 5, $$It likes to nap on the mat.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 0, $$Lara the ladybug was a special bug.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 1, $$Unlike all her friends, she had bright yellow wings.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 2, $$Everyone loved her yellow wings.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 3, $$Each morning, Bibi Butterfly said hello. Manto Mantis always waved.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 4, $$Even Sesa, the sulky spider, was happy to see her.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 5, $$At school, she played with lots of friends.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 6, $$But Lara wanted to be like the other ladybugs. “I wish I had red wings like you, Mama,” she cried.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 7, $$So one day, to cheer her up, Lara’s mother painted her wings bright red.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 8, $$The next morning, nobody greeted Lara on her way to school.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 9, $$And when she got there, none of her friends said hello.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 10, $$Lara sat all alone. No one noticed her new red wings.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 11, $$Until Miss Miya the teacher spotted Lara and said: “You’ve painted your lovely yellow wings! ”$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 12, $$Lara’s classmates were shocked. “Your wings are special! ” “So unique! ” “So rare! ”$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 13, $$"Lara,"Miss Miya said, “your yellow wings are what make you you.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 14, $$Back home, Lara took a long bath and scrubbed until her golden wings gleamed.$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 15, $$“I’ll never paint my wings again! ” she thought. Except, maybe once or twice …$$),
    ('d220d029-3e29-4b8b-bd27-660ffd55bf28', 16, $$To try a bit of purple … or something nice. But not forever and just for fun.$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 0, $$Dina woke up to a sunny day and decided, " Today, I'll explore the magical garden! "$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 1, $$As she walk her way, she saw 1 bright sun shining in the sky. " Good morning, Mr. Sun! " Dina giggled.$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 2, $$She hopped along and spotted 2 flutterring butterflies , one blue and one yellow. They danced around Dina and flew away.$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 3, $$Next, she sniffed the air and found 3 colorful flowers blooming beside the path. She sniffed each one - " Sniff! Sniff! Sniff! "$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 4, $$Then, she heard a chirp and looked around. She saw 4 singing birds on a branch. They sand a cheerful tune just for her.$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 5, $$Dina giggled and walked further, where she saw 5 juicy carrots growing in the garden.$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 6, $$Along the way, she found 6 crawling ladybugs playing hide and sees. " Peekaboo! " said Dina, giggling.$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 7, $$Near the pond there were 7 slippery frogs hopping on lily pads. " Boing! Boing! " Dina copied them.$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 8, $$Dina counted 8 busy ants marching in a line. " Left, right, left! " she cheered.$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 9, $$In a tree, she spotted 9 buzzing bees flying from flower to flower. " Buzz, buzz! Don't sting me! " she laughed.$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 10, $$And just before heading home, Dina found 10 sparkly stars starting to twinkle as night fell.$$),
    ('d4393f63-7f98-4217-b5de-f0d4c54c8397', 11, $$" What a magical day! " Dina curled up under the tree and whispered, " I counted from 1 to 10, and now...it's time to dream again. "$$),
    ('d4505e44-754c-4899-8419-bb79f5386293', 0, $$I am hungry! I want a banana!$$),
    ('d4505e44-754c-4899-8419-bb79f5386293', 1, $$I go to the tree. I pluck bananas.$$),
    ('d4505e44-754c-4899-8419-bb79f5386293', 2, $$I have bananas, now.$$),
    ('d4505e44-754c-4899-8419-bb79f5386293', 3, $$I eat a banana. I eat two bananas. I eat three bananas. I eat many bananas.$$),
    ('d4505e44-754c-4899-8419-bb79f5386293', 4, $$I am not hungry, now. I have a hundred bananas.$$),
    ('d4505e44-754c-4899-8419-bb79f5386293', 5, $$What will I do?$$),
    ('d4505e44-754c-4899-8419-bb79f5386293', 6, $$I will mix banana and sugar. I will make banana halwa!$$),
    ('d4505e44-754c-4899-8419-bb79f5386293', 7, $$I will eat banana halwa. I am happy!$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 0, $$There are so many different jobs people do! Each one helps in a special way. A teacher helps children learn new things every day.$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 1, $$A hairdresser styles and takes care of people’s hair.$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 2, $$A pilot flies airplanes high above the clouds.$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 3, $$A photographer takes beautiful pictures.$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 4, $$A paediatrician helps children feel better when they’re sick.$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 5, $$A police officer keeps people safe and helps solve crime.$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 6, $$A soccer player can play for their country in the world cup.$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 7, $$A musician sings songs that make us smile and dance.$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 8, $$An electrician makes sure the lights work at home.$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 9, $$A construction worker builds houses and schools.$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 10, $$A taxi driver takes people where they need to go.$$),
    ('d769a54d-6d41-4d64-b6a9-21bb0f0c3902', 11, $$What job have you thought of doing when you grow up?$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 0, $$There was a time when all the animals lived together as friends. One day they decided to have a meeting to elect a king.$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 1, $$Rooster wanted to be king. So he lied to the other animals. He told them, “The red comb on my head is fire! Don’t touch the comb on my head! ”$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 2, $$The other animals believed Rooster. They decided to elect Rooster as their king. The animals hoped that Rooster’s fire would help them in cold weather.$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 3, $$Then came a day when it rained. And rained. And rained. It was cold. Everything was wet and cold.$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 4, $$“Where can we get fire to warm our bodies? ” Rabbit asked the other animals.$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 5, $$“We can get fire from the comb on Rooster’s head,” replied Monkey. “Rooster is our king because he has fire on his head,” said Monkey.$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 6, $$The animals agreed with Monkey. They sent Fox to collect fire from king Rooster.$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 7, $$Fox found Rooster in a deep sleep. So he decided to take fire without asking Rooster.$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 8, $$Fox collected some dry grass. He put the grass next to the comb on Rooster’s head. Nothing happened. The grass did not catch fire.$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 9, $$“Wake up king Rooster! ” yelled Fox. “We need fire now. ”$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 10, $$But Rooster could not give fire to Fox.$$),
    ('d88e8285-fe17-4bb5-9910-9303834521ba', 11, $$Fox was angry. He went back to the other animals. He told them the truth about the comb on Rooster’s head. From that day, no one was afraid of Rooster. And foxes eat roosters and their families.$$),
    ('daef0274-25f2-4606-814a-00073065953a', 0, $$Holidays have juice of an Alphonso mango, and of never ending cool evening..$$),
    ('daef0274-25f2-4606-814a-00073065953a', 1, $$Holidays are drama after waking up but still sleeping on the pillow Holidays are islands$$),
    ('daef0274-25f2-4606-814a-00073065953a', 2, $$Holidays are gift coupons there is discount on studies and bonus on games and play Holidays are sweet and sour$$),
    ('daef0274-25f2-4606-814a-00073065953a', 3, $$That coward is the slave of a calendar May be, a holiday is a candy which dissolves soon.$$),
    ('def898a3-141b-4d2a-a98e-5cbaeb15be67', 0, $$The Lord is my shepherd, I lack nothing.$$),
    ('def898a3-141b-4d2a-a98e-5cbaeb15be67', 1, $$He takes me to lush pastures.$$),
    ('def898a3-141b-4d2a-a98e-5cbaeb15be67', 2, $$He leads me to refreshing water. He restores my strength.$$),
    ('def898a3-141b-4d2a-a98e-5cbaeb15be67', 3, $$He leads me down the right paths for the sake of his reputation.$$),
    ('def898a3-141b-4d2a-a98e-5cbaeb15be67', 4, $$Even when I must walk through the darkest valley,$$),
    ('def898a3-141b-4d2a-a98e-5cbaeb15be67', 5, $$I fear no danger, for you are with me.$$),
    ('def898a3-141b-4d2a-a98e-5cbaeb15be67', 6, $$Your rod and your staff reassure me.$$),
    ('def898a3-141b-4d2a-a98e-5cbaeb15be67', 7, $$You prepare a feast before me in plain sight of my enemies.$$),
    ('def898a3-141b-4d2a-a98e-5cbaeb15be67', 8, $$You refresh my head with oil, my cup is completely full.$$),
    ('def898a3-141b-4d2a-a98e-5cbaeb15be67', 9, $$Surely your goodness and faithfulness will pursue me all my days,$$),
    ('def898a3-141b-4d2a-a98e-5cbaeb15be67', 10, $$and I will live in the Lord’s house for the rest of my life.$$),
    ('df1160eb-c520-4a60-a97b-99f70abbc2f9', 0, $$I am an owl I see in the night....$$),
    ('df1160eb-c520-4a60-a97b-99f70abbc2f9', 1, $$…..and I sleep all the day$$),
    ('df1160eb-c520-4a60-a97b-99f70abbc2f9', 2, $$One day all the birds woke me up from the sleep.$$),
    ('df1160eb-c520-4a60-a97b-99f70abbc2f9', 3, $$Cause their friend is falling on the ground.....$$),
    ('df1160eb-c520-4a60-a97b-99f70abbc2f9', 4, $$…..and vulture moving around$$),
    ('df1160eb-c520-4a60-a97b-99f70abbc2f9', 5, $$All of us helped the bird to get on the branch$$),
    ('df1160eb-c520-4a60-a97b-99f70abbc2f9', 6, $$The peacock danced for me$$),
    ('df1160eb-c520-4a60-a97b-99f70abbc2f9', 7, $$All the birds are happy$$),
    ('df1160eb-c520-4a60-a97b-99f70abbc2f9', 8, $$I am again sleepy....$$),
    ('df171156-07f1-4336-a7c0-f868763b45da', 0, $$This is Samir. He is in class four.$$),
    ('df171156-07f1-4336-a7c0-f868763b45da', 1, $$Every morning we get ready for school. I can button my _________$$),
    ('df171156-07f1-4336-a7c0-f868763b45da', 2, $$Samir helps me put on my ________$$),
    ('df171156-07f1-4336-a7c0-f868763b45da', 3, $$Samir takes me on his ________ I ring the bell.$$),
    ('df171156-07f1-4336-a7c0-f868763b45da', 4, $$Samir reads big ________. He writes with a pen.$$),
    ('df171156-07f1-4336-a7c0-f868763b45da', 5, $$I have a small ________. Inside it are two pencils.$$),
    ('df171156-07f1-4336-a7c0-f868763b45da', 6, $$After school Samir plays ________. His three friends join him.$$),
    ('df171156-07f1-4336-a7c0-f868763b45da', 7, $$Samir hits a six. I help him find the ________.$$),
    ('df171156-07f1-4336-a7c0-f868763b45da', 8, $$He buys me an ________. It is five o'clock.$$),
    ('df171156-07f1-4336-a7c0-f868763b45da', 9, $$It is time to go ________.$$),
    ('df171156-07f1-4336-a7c0-f868763b45da', 10, $$1. Shirt 2. Shoes 3. Cycle 4. Books 5. Bag 6. Cricket 7. Ball 8. Ice-Cream$$),
    ('e2a0fdfa-8758-487b-a5b9-51a2c623d8b4', 0, $$Why should I go to school every day?$$),
    ('e2a0fdfa-8758-487b-a5b9-51a2c623d8b4', 1, $$It is good for you.$$),
    ('e2a0fdfa-8758-487b-a5b9-51a2c623d8b4', 2, $$Why should I have a bath every day?$$),
    ('e2a0fdfa-8758-487b-a5b9-51a2c623d8b4', 3, $$It is good for you.$$),
    ('e2a0fdfa-8758-487b-a5b9-51a2c623d8b4', 4, $$Why should I not play in the sun?$$),
    ('e2a0fdfa-8758-487b-a5b9-51a2c623d8b4', 5, $$It is not good for you.$$),
    ('e2a0fdfa-8758-487b-a5b9-51a2c623d8b4', 6, $$Why should I not stay up late?$$),
    ('e2a0fdfa-8758-487b-a5b9-51a2c623d8b4', 7, $$It is not good for you.$$),
    ('e2a0fdfa-8758-487b-a5b9-51a2c623d8b4', 8, $$Why should I sleep every day?$$),
    ('e2a0fdfa-8758-487b-a5b9-51a2c623d8b4', 9, $$Your body needs rest.$$),
    ('e2a0fdfa-8758-487b-a5b9-51a2c623d8b4', 10, $$Why should I listen to you? You know why.$$),
    ('e2d15511-a7cd-4ada-990d-7a70b8f00343', 0, $$Once upon a time, the animals decided to have a party. But it was not for all of them. It was only for the animals that had horns.$$),
    ('e2d15511-a7cd-4ada-990d-7a70b8f00343', 1, $$The rabbit was getting ready for the party. But then he found out that the party was not for everyone. It was just for animals with horns.$$),
    ('e2d15511-a7cd-4ada-990d-7a70b8f00343', 2, $$The rabbit went somewhere and got some horns. Then he put them on his head and went to the party.$$),
    ('e2d15511-a7cd-4ada-990d-7a70b8f00343', 3, $$During the party the rabbit ate and drank and danced.$$),
    ('e2d15511-a7cd-4ada-990d-7a70b8f00343', 4, $$This made him tired and he fell down in the sun. But while the rabbit was sleeping, the horns fell off!$$),
    ('e2d15511-a7cd-4ada-990d-7a70b8f00343', 5, $$Then all the animals discovered that the rabbit was not the kind of animal they wanted. So they pulled his ears till they got bigger and bigger.$$),
    ('e2d15511-a7cd-4ada-990d-7a70b8f00343', 6, $$Then they ran away. And that’s the reason why rabbits have big ears!$$),
    ('e5e7a4e1-7ee4-4b5c-95b2-96b2d69a1729', 0, $$Do you know the story of Joseph and Mary? They traveled to Bethlehem in a bit of a hurry.$$),
    ('e5e7a4e1-7ee4-4b5c-95b2-96b2d69a1729', 1, $$It was time for Mary to give birth to a baby. The innkeeper asked, “Could you sleep in here, maybe? ”$$),
    ('e5e7a4e1-7ee4-4b5c-95b2-96b2d69a1729', 2, $$Near the animals’ manger, the baby was born. They wrapped him in cloth, and he slept until morn.$$),
    ('e5e7a4e1-7ee4-4b5c-95b2-96b2d69a1729', 3, $$Shepherds were staying in the fields out of town. Then an angel appeared and God’s glory shone down.$$),
    ('e5e7a4e1-7ee4-4b5c-95b2-96b2d69a1729', 4, $$He said, “Don’t be afraid, I bring you great news. A Saviour is born! There’s no time to lose! ”$$),
    ('e5e7a4e1-7ee4-4b5c-95b2-96b2d69a1729', 5, $$Then so many angels filled the night sky, saying, “Peace on Earth! Glory to God on high! ”$$),
    ('e5e7a4e1-7ee4-4b5c-95b2-96b2d69a1729', 6, $$The shepherds were shocked, and their world was rocked. “Let’s go find this baby! ” they said to the flock.$$),
    ('e5e7a4e1-7ee4-4b5c-95b2-96b2d69a1729', 7, $$They found Mary and Joseph where the angel said. Baby Jesus was wrapped up, with a manger for a bed.$$),
    ('e5e7a4e1-7ee4-4b5c-95b2-96b2d69a1729', 8, $$Then the shepherds spread the news of this wonderful story: A Saviour in the hay and a sky filled with glory!$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 0, $$To kill a baboon, you must have dry eyes.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 1, $$The dog that’s full doesn’t bite.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 2, $$When hippos fight, it’s the grass that suffers.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 3, $$The chick dirties the nest because that’s what she sees her mother do.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 4, $$A frog and a toad are both born the same way.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 5, $$A single fingernail cannot kill a louse.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 6, $$The lion that doesn’t have meat eats grass.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 7, $$The little goat in the back is the one that gets the stick.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 8, $$You’re afraid of the dark when there are not even hyenas.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 9, $$The lizard dies of shame.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 10, $$To see the eyes of a snail is to have patience.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 11, $$You despised the tortoise, but he’s the one that has water.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 12, $$The hyena that howls in the fields does not eat millet.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 13, $$The visitor is the one that kills the snake.$$),
    ('e6198cba-b698-4dd6-a486-e71d4f3babf2', 14, $$Don’t say that there’s an elephant over there when you’re on the shoulders.$$),
    ('ef4f0b8a-b605-47e8-aac2-3319591c6b9c', 0, $$The big wave washed the shells to the shore.$$),
    ('ef4f0b8a-b605-47e8-aac2-3319591c6b9c', 1, $$The big wave washed the boat out into the ocean.$$),
    ('ef4f0b8a-b605-47e8-aac2-3319591c6b9c', 2, $$The big wave splashed on the beach and make the children wet.$$),
    ('ef4f0b8a-b605-47e8-aac2-3319591c6b9c', 3, $$The big wave rolled the nets on the reef.$$),
    ('ef4f0b8a-b605-47e8-aac2-3319591c6b9c', 4, $$I love swimming in the big wave.$$),
    ('ef4f0b8a-b605-47e8-aac2-3319591c6b9c', 5, $$The End!$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 0, $$These are my big brother Remo’s shoes.$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 1, $$Look what I can do in them.$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 2, $$I can race cars!$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 3, $$Sometimes, I race our dog.$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 4, $$When I wear Remo’s shoes I win every time.$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 5, $$Wait! Let me show you one more thing.$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 6, $$Watch me dance and spin.$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 7, $$I can do a handstand and walk on my hands.$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 8, $$I’m a flying fox! Look at me hang upside down.$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 9, $$Watch me jump and touch the moon.$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 10, $$Here, try them on!$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 11, $$See what you can do in Remo’s shoes.$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 12, $$$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 13, $$$$),
    ('f25fe9f8-a91e-441b-92e1-6001ec356941', 14, $$$$),
    ('fc73d674-4519-4929-9c13-c74d50f15521', 0, $$This is a family .$$),
    ('fc73d674-4519-4929-9c13-c74d50f15521', 1, $$This is a mother.$$),
    ('fc73d674-4519-4929-9c13-c74d50f15521', 2, $$This is a son.$$),
    ('fc73d674-4519-4929-9c13-c74d50f15521', 3, $$This is a father.$$),
    ('fc73d674-4519-4929-9c13-c74d50f15521', 4, $$This is a daughter$$),
    ('fc73d674-4519-4929-9c13-c74d50f15521', 5, $$These are siblings.$$),
    ('fc73d674-4519-4929-9c13-c74d50f15521', 6, $$This is a grandmother.$$),
    ('fc73d674-4519-4929-9c13-c74d50f15521', 7, $$This is a grandfather.$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 0, $$Kila the Village Hero$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 1, $$Kila grew up on the beautiful island of Manus.$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 2, $$When Kila was five she became very sick with polio. She was no longer able to walk.$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 3, $$Kila's mother carried her back and forth to school. Other children in the village made fun of her. They laughed at her.$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 4, $$Kila loved to play. She could not play on the ground, but she could play in the water. Kila could swim like a fish.$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 5, $$One day Kila heard a shout, "Help! "$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 6, $$She could see little Johnny out in the water. He was about to drown!$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 7, $$Kila swam as fast as she could to reach Johnny. She held him up and together they swam to the shore.$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 8, $$Johnny's family, and everyone in the village, came to the shore to watch.$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 9, $$Kila arrived at the shore with Johnny. People were cheering and shouting.$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 10, $$Kila was the hero of the day.$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 11, $$The next day there was a big feast. Kila had saved little Johnny's life.$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 12, $$The children never made fun of Kila again.$$),
    ('fef29f44-f0ac-4bc4-a12e-ae554180af12', 13, $$Workshop for the Deaf and Blind - September 2021$$)
  ) AS v(source_id, page_index, text)
  JOIN books b
    ON b.source_platform = 'bloom' AND b.source_id = v.source_id
ON CONFLICT (book_id, page_index) DO NOTHING;

